# Personal-data patterns for githooks/pre-commit.
#
# Copy to `.pii-patterns` (gitignored) and replace the placeholders with the
# real names you need to keep out of this public repo. Do NOT put real values
# in THIS file -- it is tracked, so anything here gets published.
#
# One extended regex (ERE) per line. Matching is case-insensitive. Blank lines
# and lines starting with # are ignored. Patterns are checked against both the
# staged diff's added lines and the staged filenames.
#
# Keep them specific: a pattern like `notes` would match half the repo and
# train you to bypass the hook, which is worse than having no hook.

# The student's given name, as it appears in folder names.
StudentGivenName

# The coaching institute / programme, and its batch codes.
InstituteName
Programme-Study-[0-9]+th-[0-9]{2}-[0-9]{2}

# The personal Drive folder tree, e.g. "NNN-Education/NN-Somebody" where NNN
# is the real numeric prefix. (Written with N placeholders on purpose: spelling
# the real digits out here would trip this very pattern -- as it did once.)
[0-9]{3}-Education

# The transcript source folder, if its name identifies a batch or channel.
Lecture-Channel-Download
